  "body_html": "<h1>Block Induction Setup</h1>\n<p>For a datum \\(\\Sigma\\) with positive-depth blocks, split off the highest-depth block:\n\\[\n\\Sigma={}^{b}\\Sigma\\oplus{}^{a}\\Sigma,\\qquad\nV={}^{b}V\\oplus{}^{a}V,\\qquad\n\\Gamma={}^{b}\\Gamma\\oplus{}^{a}\\Gamma.\n\\]\nLet \\(r\\) be the highest depth and \\(s=r/2\\). The compact subgroup and type decompose into block-diagonal and off-diagonal parts:\n\\[\nK=(^{b}K\\times{}^{a}K)\\,{}^{\\boxminus}J,\\qquad\nK_+=(^{b}K_+\\times{}^{a}K_+)\\,{}^{\\boxminus}J_+.\n\\]\nThe off-diagonal quotient\n\\[\n{}^{\\boxminus}W={}^\\boxminus J/{}^\\boxminus J_+\n\\]\nis a finite symplectic space, and Yu's construction factors the positive-depth representation as\n\\[\n\\kappa={}^\\boxplus\\kappa\\otimes{}^\\boxminus\\kappa,\\qquad\n\\eta={}^\\boxplus\\eta\\otimes{}^\\boxminus\\kappa.\n\\]</p>",
